<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 59,400 in April.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 59,400 in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in April and average earnings in March.</p>
<p> UNEMPLOYMENT		    APRIL	 MARCH   (PREL MARCH)</p>
<p> Monthly change		 -59,400	-37,300    (-41,100)</p>
<p> Rate (pct)			5.9*	  6.1		(6.1)</p>
<p> Monthly non-s/adj change   -57,300	n/a	  (-82,500)</p>
<p> Monthly non-s/adj rate	6.0	   6.2		(6.2)</p>
<p>NOTE - Markets forecast 40,000 April unemployment fall</p>
<p> Unemployment level (mln)    1,651*	1,711	  (1,707)</p>
<p> Unemployment level unadj    1,688	 1,745	  (1,745)</p>
<p> Avg change in past 3m adj  -54,400     -57,400     (-58,700)</p>
<p> Avg change in past 6m	-62,300     -60,000     (-60,600)</p>
<p> AVERAGE EARNINGS		MARCH	 FEB	 (PREL FEB)</p>
<p> underlying yearly chng (%)  4.5	   4.5		(5.0)</p>
<p> index (base 1990)	     136.9	 136.0	  (136.0)</p>
<p> actual yearly chng (%)	4.4	   4.1		(4.1)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p> Production -- underlying    4.5	   4.25	    (4.75)</p>
<p>		-- actual	  3.8	   4.3		(4.1)</p>
<p> Manufacturing -- underlying 4.75	  4.5	     (4.75)</p>
<p>		   -- actual     4.1	   4.6		(4.4)</p>
<p> Services   -- underlying    4.75	  4.75	     (5.0)</p>
<p>		-- actual	  5.0	   4.2		(4.2)</p>
<p>NOTE: Consensus forecast 5.0 percent for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p> UNIT WAGE COSTS		 MARCH	 FEB	 (PREL FEB)</p>
<p> Monthly change vs yr ago    2.3**	 2.8		(2.4)</p>
<p> Index (base=1990)	     115.6	 115.8	  (115.4)</p>
<p> 3-mth versus same yr/ago    2.6	   2.7		(2.6)</p>
<p> Index (base=1990)	     115.5	 115.6	  (115.4)</p>
<p>PRODUCTIVITY</p>
<p> Monthly change vs yr/ago    1.7	   1.7		(1.8)</p>
<p> Index (base=1990)	     122.7	 122.7	  (122.8)</p>
<p> 3-mth versus same yr/ago    1.7	   1.8		(1.9)</p>
<p> Index (base=1990)	     122.5	 122.3	  (122.4)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT (THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p> WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT     Q4	    Q3	     Q4 1995</p>
<p> level			     26,147	26,100	  25,925</p>
<p> change			    47	    216		  148</p>
<p>EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT</p>
<p> level			     22,363	22,308	  22,142</p>
<p> change			    54	    115		  145</p>
<p> JOB CENTRE VACANCIES	  APRIL	 MARCH   (PREL MARCH)</p>
<p> change			     +300	+3,700	 (+3,500)</p>
<p> level			     275,600     275,300    (275,100)</p>
<p> Avg 3m change		   +4,200     +3,000	 (+2,900)</p>
<p>* The ONS said the 5.9 percent unemployment rate was last lower in September 1990 when it was 5.8 pct, the level of unemployment was last lower in August 1990 when it was 1,642,000.</p>
<p>** The ONS said unit wage costs growth was the lowest since May 1995.</p>
<p>Unemployment figures continue to be affected by the Jobseekers Allowance, due to changes in operational procedures.  </p>
<p>But the ONS said the recorded unemployment falls over the last six months suggest the rate of fall is faster than in mid-1996 -- in other words, higher than the 15-20,000 per month previously reported.</p>
<p>The ONS said the downward revisions to average earnings were due to revised data and a downward revision to estimates of bonus payments.</p>
